IMPORT prelude

-- People's Association Act 1960 (Singapore) -- the offence of using a symbol like the Association's (s 15), the good-faith bar on
-- suits against those who act for it (s 10), certificates of proficiency (s 9(i)), who sits on the Association and its Board and
-- for how long (ss 4, 5 and the Schedule), how its meetings are called, presided over, made quorate and decided (s 6), how its seal
-- is executed (s 11), where its moneys may be deposited (s 13(1)), and its financial year (s 14).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/PAA1960.txt. The deposit says it "incorporates all
-- amendments up to and including 1 December 2021 and comes into operation on 31 December 2021", and its page furniture reads
-- "Informal Consolidation -- version in force from 14/4/2025". The latest amendment annotated is S 267/2025, which deleted item 4
-- of the Schedule with effect from 14 April 2025; ss 5A, 7 and 16 carry [5/2018]. The deposit's metadata calls it the current
-- version as at 5 October 2026.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0198 in subjects/sg/requirements.jsonl: tier 3 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. The requirement asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked
-- a sharper question yet. The Act is short (16 sections and a Schedule) and mostly constitutes the Association, so this row takes
-- the two provisions that reach outsiders (ss 15 and 10), the one that reaches course participants (s 9(i)), and the constitutional
-- rules that can be computed.
--
-- Not encoded: the objects (s 8) and the Board's general powers (s 9 other than para (i)), which confer discretion and decide
-- nothing for an outsider; Ministerial directions (s 5A) and disclosure of interest (s 7), which work through the Public Sector
-- (Governance) Act 2018 (not read); share issues to the Minister for Finance (s 13A); investment (s 13(4)); accounts opened in a
-- committee's name (s 13(2)); the Chief Executive (s 16); the names of the 84 member organisations beyond their count.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `People's Association Act 1960`

§§ `15 -- the Association's symbols`

-- s 15(1): the Association "has the exclusive right to the use of such symbols ... as it may devise or adopt from time to time and
-- thereafter display or exhibit in connection with its activities or affairs". (2): it "must publish the Association's symbols in
-- the Gazette". (3): "Any person who uses a symbol identical with, or which so resembles, any of the Association's symbols as to be
-- likely to deceive or cause confusion, shall be guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding
-- $10,000."
--
-- Reading taken: "as to be likely to deceive or cause confusion" attaches to "so resembles"; an identical symbol is caught without
-- more. Gazette publication is a duty in (2), not a condition of the offence in (3) -- the text does not link them. There is no
-- exception for use with the Association's permission on the face of s 15.
GIVEN `devised or adopted by the Association` IS A BOOLEAN, `displayed in connection with its activities` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the symbol is one of the Association's symbols` IF
    `devised or adopted by the Association` AND `displayed in connection with its activities`

GIVEN `uses the symbol` IS A BOOLEAN, `identical to an Association symbol` IS A BOOLEAN, `resembles one so as to be likely to deceive or confuse` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `using the symbol is an offence` IF
    `uses the symbol` AND (`identical to an Association symbol` OR `resembles one so as to be likely to deceive or confuse`)

GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine for misusing a symbol` MEANS 10000

GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `imprisonment is available for misusing a symbol` IF FALSE

§§ `10 -- protection from personal liability`

-- s 10: "No suit or other legal proceedings shall lie against -- (a) any member, officer or employee of the Association or any other
-- person acting under the direction of the Association; (b) any member of the Board or any person acting under the direction of
-- the Board; or (c) any member or officer of any committee appointed by the Board or any person acting under the direction of such
-- committee, for anything which is in good faith done or intended to be done in the execution or purported execution of this Act."
-- s 2(3): the Association itself "may sue and be sued in its corporate name". s 10 does not protect the Association.
DECLARE Defendant IS ONE OF
    `a member of the Association`
    `an employee of the Association`
    `a volunteer acting under the Association's direction`
    `a member of the Board`
    `a member of a committee appointed by the Board`
    `a person acting under a committee's direction`
    `the Association itself`
    `a volunteer acting on his or her own initiative`

GIVEN `the defendant` IS A Defendant
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the defendant is within section 10` IF
    CONSIDER `the defendant`
    WHEN `the Association itself` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a volunteer acting on his or her own initiative` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the defendant` IS A Defendant, `acted in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN, `in execution or purported execution of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the suit is barred` IF
    `the defendant is within section 10` `the defendant` AND `acted in good faith` AND `in execution or purported execution of the Act`

§§ `9(i) -- certificates of proficiency`

-- s 9(i): the Board may "award certificates of proficiency to persons who attend any of the courses or activities organised by the
-- Association, after tests approved by the Association". A power, not a duty: this decides only eligibility.
GIVEN `attended a course or activity organised by the Association` IS A BOOLEAN, `passed a test approved by the Association` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a certificate of proficiency may be awarded` IF
    `attended a course or activity organised by the Association` AND `passed a test approved by the Association`

§§ `4, 5 and the Schedule -- membership of the Association and the Board`

-- s 4(1): the Association consists of (a) the Prime Minister as Chairperson; (b) a Minister appointed as Deputy Chairperson; (c) 8
-- members appointed by the Chairperson; and (d) one member appointed in consultation with each organisation in the Schedule.
-- The Schedule numbers 85 organisations; item 4 is "[Deleted by S 267/2025 wef 14/04/2025]", leaving 84.
-- s 5(1): the Board consists of the persons in s 4(1)(a), (b) and (c) and "4 members to be elected from among themselves by the
-- persons mentioned in section 4(1)(d)". s 4(5): the Board may by Gazette notification vary the number of its members and amend
-- the Schedule -- so these are the counts the text gives, not fixed numbers.
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the number of member organisations in the Schedule` MEANS 85 MINUS 1

GIVEN `organisations in the Schedule` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the number of members of the Association` `organisations in the Schedule` MEANS 1 PLUS 1 PLUS 8 PLUS `organisations in the Schedule`

GIVETH A NUMBER
`the number of members of the Board` MEANS 1 PLUS 1 PLUS 8 PLUS 4

-- s 4(2): the Chairperson "may revoke any appointment at any time without assigning any reason". (3): appointees "hold office for a
-- period of 3 years" and are eligible for re-appointment. (6), (7): a person filling a vacancy "holds office for so long as the
-- member in whose place he or she is appointed would have held office".
GIVEN `year appointed` IS A NUMBER, `fills a vacancy` IS A BOOLEAN, `year the predecessor was appointed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the year the appointment ends` `year appointed` `fills a vacancy` `year the predecessor was appointed` MEANS
    IF `fills a vacancy` THEN `year the predecessor was appointed` PLUS 3 ELSE `year appointed` PLUS 3

-- s 5(3): elected Board members "hold office for a period of 3 years from the date of their election". (4): the term "ceases upon
-- the revocation of his or her appointment as a member of the Association under section 4(2), or if his or her appointment as a
-- member of the Association has expired and he or she has not been re-appointed".
GIVEN `years since election` IS A NUMBER, `Association appointment revoked` IS A BOOLEAN, `Association appointment expired` IS A BOOLEAN, `re-appointed to the Association` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the elected Board member still holds office` IF
        `years since election` LESS THAN 3
    AND (NOT `Association appointment revoked`)
    AND (NOT (`Association appointment expired` AND (NOT `re-appointed to the Association`)))

§§ `6 -- meetings`

-- s 6(1): the Board "must in any case meet at least once in 3 months". (2): the Board "must in any case convene a general meeting
-- once in every 3 years".
GIVEN `months since the last Board meeting` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Board is overdue to meet` IF `months since the last Board meeting` GREATER THAN 3

-- s 6(3): the Board must send "to all members of the Association" a notice giving "at least 7 days' notice", "specifying the date,
-- time and place of the meeting and the business to be transacted thereat". Whether the 7 days are clear days the text does not
-- say; this file counts days from sending to the meeting.
GIVEN `days between sending and the meeting` IS A NUMBER, `sent to all members` IS A BOOLEAN, `states date, time and place` IS A BOOLEAN, `states the business` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the general meeting notice complies` IF
        `days between sending and the meeting` AT LEAST 7
    AND `sent to all members`
    AND `states date, time and place`
    AND `states the business`

-- s 6(4): notice "is deemed to have been received by a member if sent by ordinary post or despatched by messenger to the address of
-- the member as stated in the records of the Association". Email is not mentioned: it earns no deeming (it may still be received).
DECLARE `Means of sending` IS ONE OF
    `ordinary post`
    `messenger`
    `email`

GIVEN `means` IS A `Means of sending`, `to the address in the Association's records` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the member is deemed to have received the notice` IF
    `to the address in the Association's records` AND
        CONSIDER `means`
        WHEN `ordinary post` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `messenger` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 6(5): the Chairperson presides; (6) the Deputy Chairperson in the Chairperson's absence; (7) in the absence of both, "any member
-- that the members present may select acts as Chairperson".
DECLARE Presider IS ONE OF
    `the Chairperson`
    `the Deputy Chairperson`
    `a member selected by those present`

GIVEN `Chairperson present` IS A BOOLEAN, `Deputy Chairperson present` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A Presider
`who presides` `Chairperson present` `Deputy Chairperson present` MEANS
    IF `Chairperson present` THEN `the Chairperson`
    ELSE IF `Deputy Chairperson present` THEN `the Deputy Chairperson`
         ELSE `a member selected by those present`

-- s 6(8): "The quorum at all meetings of the Association is one-third of the total number of members". (9): "The quorum at every
-- meeting of the Board is 5 members". Reading taken: one-third is a floor, so 31 of 94 (31.33 needed) is short.
GIVEN `members present` IS A NUMBER, `total members` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Association meeting is quorate` IF `members present` TIMES 3 AT LEAST `total members`

GIVEN `Board members present` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Board meeting is quorate` IF `Board members present` AT LEAST 5

-- s 6(10): questions are "decided by a majority of the members present and voting", and on "an equality of votes, the person
-- presiding at the meeting has a second or casting vote". s 6(5)(b): the Chairperson also has the right to vote. Abstainers do not
-- count.
GIVEN `votes for` IS A NUMBER, `votes against` IS A NUMBER, `presider's casting vote is for` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the question is carried` IF
        `votes for` GREATER THAN `votes against`
    OR  (`votes for` EQUALS `votes against` AND `presider's casting vote is for`)

§§ `11 -- execution of documents`

-- s 11(1): instruments requiring the seal "must be sealed with the common seal of the Association in the presence of the Chairperson
-- or the Deputy Chairperson and one other member of the Board, who must sign".
GIVEN `sealed with the common seal` IS A BOOLEAN, `Chairperson or Deputy present and signing` IS A BOOLEAN, `another Board member present and signing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the sealing complies` IF
    `sealed with the common seal` AND `Chairperson or Deputy present and signing` AND `another Board member present and signing`

§§ `13(1) -- where moneys may be deposited`

-- s 13(1): the Board may deposit the Association's moneys with "(a) any bank or banks licensed under the Banking Act 1970; or (b) any
-- finance company or companies licensed under the Finance Companies Act 1967".
DECLARE Depository IS ONE OF
    `a bank licensed under the Banking Act 1970`
    `a finance company licensed under the Finance Companies Act 1967`
    `an unlicensed overseas bank`

GIVEN `the depository` IS A Depository
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Association may deposit there` IF
    CONSIDER `the depository`
    WHEN `an unlicensed overseas bank` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `14 -- the financial year`

-- s 14: "The financial year of the Association begins on 1 April of each year and ends on 31 March of the succeeding year." This
-- gives the calendar year in which the financial year containing a date began.
GIVEN `month` IS A NUMBER, `calendar year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the year the financial year began` `month` `calendar year` MEANS
    IF `month` AT LEAST 4 THEN `calendar year` ELSE `calendar year` MINUS 1
